{
 "iona": {
  "A different relay follows S equals four times k plus three and needs fifteen. Take away the three: twelve remain. Divide by four: three coils. Check: four times three plus three is fifteen. Our relay follows five times k plus two and needs twenty two.": "iona/2dccd23fb685b145.m4a",
  "A different tank has forty litres capacity and is half full, so it holds twenty litres. A reserve of twenty five percent of its capacity is ten litres. For our tank, find one quarter of eighty litres. Three quarters are inside. Keep one quarter, then subtract the outlets.": "iona/29107efbae940f38.m4a",
  "Choose an extra repair. Water can power the letter room door or the boat lift. Each repair needs at least twelve litres. Your plan must also supply the lighthouse and leave emergency water in the tank.": "iona/d51d36ef686f47d1.m4a",
  "Eight times six is forty eight. Fifty three minus forty eight leaves five. Eight full crates and one partly filled crate make nine crates. We will load this plan together.": "iona/e7c91b3aa88756e4.m4a",
  "Eight times six is forty eight. Nothing is left over. Exactly eight crates are needed, with no extra crate. We will load this plan together.": "iona/133eb217900f94e1.m4a",
  "Eighty times three quarters is sixty litres. The reserve is eighty divided by four: twenty litres. After twenty four litres of cooling, thirty six remain. A twelve litre repair leaves twenty four litres, four above the reserve.": "iona/6023037ec5dcb414.m4a",
  "Every item has a place within the limit. The plan is ready. Thank you for giving these words a way out of the harbour.": "iona/44fb2b24074c60ed.m4a",
  "Four times eight is thirty two. Thirty eight minus thirty two leaves six maps. Four full cases and one partly filled case make five cases. We will pack this plan together.": "iona/aa888eaf62e9f51d.m4a",
  "Here is a different bundle of twenty messages. Each crate holds six. Three full crates hold eighteen. Two messages remain, so they need one more crate. Four crates send every message. Three times six plus two is twenty.": "iona/91cc9981bea514be.m4a",
  "How much water will you send to your chosen repair? Each repair needs at least twelve litres. If you chose both, this amount goes to each one. Check that your whole plan leaves the emergency water in the tank. Then press Send the water.": "iona/e40ca9f0ccfa0ad4.m4a",
  "I kept these dry for the people who wrote them. They were never mine to lock away.": "iona/0d47ad67ad5a095f.m4a",
  "Multiply your full groups by the capacity. Take that many away from the total to find the remainder. The remainder must be smaller than the capacity. If anything remains, it needs space too. If nothing remains, do not add another container.": "iona/eb45db48d623d599.m4a",
  "Now choose how much water to send from the tank to the big lighthouse. It needs at least twenty four litres to cool the light inside it. Leave enough in the tank for emergencies and your extra repair.": "iona/3285ca01e77dee12.m4a",
  "One last job. The relay needs a signal of exactly twenty two to reach the northern boats.": "iona/007930be48010f7b.m4a",
  "Our relay adds two once. Twenty two minus two leaves twenty. Each coil adds five. How many fives make twenty? Then set the dial to the strength those coils make.": "iona/4d2dc4ec4ef2d339.m4a",
  "Rest at the chamber checkpoint. Four cells make sixteen strength for the first barrier. One cell makes seven for the second. Both barriers break before a counter pulse, and one cell remains. We will make these predictions together.": "iona/841a78c9a5e312e8.m4a",
  "Seven times six is forty two. Forty seven minus forty two leaves five. Seven full crates and one partly filled crate make eight crates. Every message can go aboard. We will load this plan together.": "iona/f37ec113e190ff55.m4a",
  "Some water must stay in the tank for emergencies. Keep twenty five percent of the full eighty litres. How many litres must stay in the tank?": "iona/472bbb48832095bb.m4a",
  "That signal was the wrong strength. Wind the relay spring, and we can send another.": "iona/6b056d737fbd012f.m4a",
  "The big lighthouse needs water to cool the light inside it. The small round tank beside the crossing has the water. We will send it through the pipes, keeping some in the tank for emergencies.": "iona/d8a629eb329d6dc7.m4a",
  "The chart room has maps to protect. Each case has a limit. Plan the full cases, the maps left over, and the smallest total of cases that will protect every map.": "iona/2a561e1db4d2bebb.m4a",
  "The glass lens inside the lighthouse needs a mixture of two liquids. Amber and clear liquid must keep the stated ratio and fill the capsule to its required total. First compare a part with the whole mixture.": "iona/fb4f3f24e9bd151b.m4a",
  "The light inside the lighthouse has gone out. Please leave the letter room alone. The paper letters in there are important.": "iona/5207670b2b5d340e.m4a",
  "The loading rail is held. Every item is safe. Unload the rail once, then revise the plan. We have sent nothing away.": "iona/eb0a9e410950599b.m4a",
  "The machine adds three strength for each power cell. Its starter adds four strength once. One cell makes seven. Two make ten. Three make thirteen. E is the pulse strength. n is the number of cells. E equals three times n plus four.": "iona/6130233d13081bb0.m4a",
  "The northern boats need a signal of exactly twenty two. Choose how many coils to switch on, then set the dial to the strength they will make. Sending uses the spring; a wrong signal can be rewound.": "iona/c758f5b7a38cf0a1.m4a",
  "The relay answers. Every boat in the north will see our light tonight.": "iona/923ac1e9d52f1927.m4a",
  "The reserve uses the full eighty litres. Eighty divided by four gives one quarter. Multiply that by three for the current content. Keep one part in the tank. Subtract the cooling and repair outlets, then compare what remains with the reserve.": "iona/5c7b8dbb6c5210f7.m4a",
  "The small round tank can fit eighty litres. It is three quarters full. How much water is in the tank now? Enter the amount in litres.": "iona/8ccfe541de2ed9da.m4a",
  "There are two plus three, or five equal parts. forty divided by five gives one part. Use two parts for amber and three for clear. Check the amounts add to forty. Amber is two fifths of the whole.": "iona/9ada1bf516ae4037.m4a",
  "There are two plus three, or five equal parts. thirty divided by five gives one part. Use two parts for amber and three for clear. Check the amounts add to thirty. Amber is two fifths of the whole.": "iona/1375c1882bc413e1.m4a",
  "These messages have waited in the archive. Help me send all the messages aboard. A full crate has no empty slots. Capacity means the most it can hold. First plan the full crates, then what is left, then the smallest total we need.": "iona/0d2a904e6f462ecf.m4a",
  "This machine sends a burst of light, called a pulse. Use it to break two barriers inside the lighthouse. First, choose a rule and predict a test pulse.": "iona/33f3d0961e88c2b5.m4a",
  "This one is my own farewell. I think I can open it now.": "iona/11f30b69cfa16101.m4a",
  "Three n plus four means three times n, then add four once. It is different from three times the sum of n and four. For two cells, three times two plus four makes ten. Use this order for your new prediction.": "iona/5502d9dfbc0f02e3.m4a",
  "Three times five is fifteen. Add the four point starter to make nineteen strength. We will make this test together.": "iona/4c5baebb91a81aa6.m4a",
  "Three times four is twelve. Add the four point starter to make sixteen strength. We will make this test together.": "iona/1c885d61ee27cb7f.m4a",
  "Three times six is eighteen. Add the four point starter to make twenty two strength. We will make this test together.": "iona/30f5769ecfa02013.m4a",
  "Twenty two minus two is twenty. Twenty divided by five is four coils. Check: five times four plus two equals twenty two. Switch on four coils and set the dial to twenty two. We will send it together.": "iona/8cef4a7eb632d4b9.m4a",
  "Two Grey barriers block the lens. Choose cells for a light pulse and predict its strength. Casting uses up those cells. A barrier that survives sends a counter pulse. You can plan without a timer.": "iona/c8023977ec1d3569.m4a",
  "Two amber parts and three clear parts make five equal parts. In a ten millilitre sample, each part is two millilitres. Four amber plus six clear make ten. Amber is two fifths of the whole; two to three compares amber with clear.": "iona/e431ebe13e5ca831.m4a",
  "Use four cells. Three times four plus four is sixteen. We will cast this pulse together.": "iona/a9a3451898f4acf6.m4a",
  "Use one cells. Three times one plus four is seven. We will cast this pulse together.": "iona/ca23695e68a4f065.m4a",
  "Use three cells. Three times three plus four is thirteen. We will cast this pulse together.": "iona/e8b0c6b8b398826b.m4a",
  "Use two cells. Three times two plus four is ten. We will cast this pulse together.": "iona/7ef02a3c55d50187.m4a",
  "Water was getting into the letter room. It could ruin people’s paper letters. I changed the pipes to keep the letters dry. That stopped cooling water reaching the lighthouse too. I meant to fix it before anyone needed the light.": "iona/5bd92168805eb48f.m4a",
  "forty divided by five is eight millilitres per part. Two parts give sixteen millilitres amber; three give twenty four clear. Together they make forty. Amber is two fifths of the whole. We will pour this one together.": "iona/506218c5601007e8.m4a",
  "forty eight divided by four gives twelve millilitres per part. Amber uses twelve millilitres, clear uses thirty six. Amber is one out of four equal parts of the whole. This is a worked plan.": "iona/a753bc0fd1441875.m4a",
  "one hundred and sixty litres times three divided by four gives one hundred and twenty litres inside. twenty five percent of full capacity is forty litres of reserve. Plan A leaves fifty six litres, enough to protect the reserve. This is a worked plan.": "iona/348941cfbcf15b64.m4a",
  "one hundred and twenty litres times three divided by four gives ninety litres inside. twenty five percent of full capacity is thirty litres of reserve. Plan A leaves forty eight litres, enough to protect the reserve. This is a worked plan.": "iona/c7455efdf5b4b173.m4a",
  "one hundred litres times four divided by five gives eighty litres inside. thirty percent of full capacity is thirty litres of reserve. Plan A leaves forty litres, enough to protect the reserve. This is a worked plan.": "iona/9df7842a4b475246.m4a",
  "sixty four divided by eight gives eight millilitres per part. Amber uses twenty four millilitres, clear uses forty. Amber is three out of eight equal parts of the whole. This is a worked plan.": "iona/084b14d8ddd26fb5.m4a",
  "thirty divided by five is six millilitres per part. Two parts give twelve millilitres amber; three give eighteen clear. Together they make thirty. Amber is two fifths of the whole. We will pour this one together.": "iona/77e0e0f910ad52dc.m4a",
  "thirty five divided by five gives seven millilitres per part. Amber uses twenty one millilitres, clear uses fourteen. Amber is three out of five equal parts of the whole. This is a worked plan.": "iona/1173ffd8a131e3ce.m4a",
  "three hundred and eighty five plus twenty plus twenty is four hundred and twenty five centimetres. The stock is six hundred, so the offcut is one hundred and seventy five centimetres. This is a worked plan.": "iona/3be8e311bb8f4c6a.m4a",
  "three hundred and ten plus fifteen plus fifteen is three hundred and forty centimetres. The stock is five hundred and twenty, so the offcut is one hundred and eighty centimetres. This is a worked plan.": "iona/cf7a9063dc9781e6.m4a",
  "two hundred and seventy five plus twenty five plus twenty five is three hundred and twenty five centimetres. The stock is four hundred and sixty, so the offcut is one hundred and thirty five centimetres. This is a worked plan.": "iona/0cb36bcf3aca52b5.m4a"
 },
 "ambrose": {
  "I remembered the promise. I forgot the people it was meant to help.": "ambrose/8c5cecb4b3805799.m4a",
  "I should have told you about the bypass on the first night. No more secrets on this road.": "ambrose/eab7e5c2ccd4bc1c.m4a",
  "I will. Every part of it.": "ambrose/6ea59b8307eea31d.m4a",
  "The crossing is broken. We need a plank to reach the pump court. The plank must cover the water and rest on both stone supports.": "ambrose/f067a111d2646b5a.m4a",
  "The example gap is two metres. Add ten centimetres at each end: two point two metres. Four metres of stock minus two point two leaves one point eight metres. On our crossing, add both bearings, then subtract the cut from the stock.": "ambrose/128448899f84d768.m4a",
  "The gap is only the water. The timber must also rest on land.": "ambrose/b352027b97f89ed9.m4a",
  "The leftover is the wood that remains after cutting your plank. Work out its length so we can label it for later use. The full piece and your planned plank length stay on screen. No cut has been made.": "ambrose/9f786f1bbd8ef693.m4a",
  "The light inside the big lighthouse has gone out. Water from the small round tank keeps that light cool. First, we need a way across.": "ambrose/0a463181321f6262.m4a",
  "Two point eight five plus zero point two is three point zero five. Add the other zero point two: three point two five metres. Four point eight minus three point two five leaves one point five five metres. We will make this cut together.": "ambrose/8d55d8e93790f095.m4a",
  "Your Gran and I built a bypass. I thought keeping that secret would keep her route safe.": "ambrose/1c97a9dda45307b0.m4a",
  "Your Gran once mended this harbour with me. Her last route is kept inside the lighthouse.": "ambrose/e02575113fd0b5f9.m4a"
 },
 "narrator": {
  "A lit shelter waits beside the wharf. This is a good place to stop for tonight.": "narrator/88cad97a7fda1d3f.m4a",
  "The ferry lift raises the message boat. Its crew wait at the wharf for the harbour’s letters.": "narrator/dcd16e434f2173bb.m4a",
  "The letter room door opens. The paper letters are dry. Iona carries the letters down to the wharf herself.": "narrator/1b89da5eaff1e7e2.m4a",
  "The northern lens turns. Light runs out across the water, and the Grey draws back from the harbour.": "narrator/24620d62805f99d6.m4a"
 },
 "girl": {
  "Then stay beside me, and tell me everything you remember about Gran.": "girl/9d82c6f61115e89c.m4a",
  "There. Gran left her mark on the road north.": "girl/d5bc713863c0066b.m4a",
  "Who would want to wipe a road off the map?": "girl/392c681f5af8a11c.m4a"
 },
 "gran": {
  "I am going north on purpose. Something taken from the map makers has to go back to them.": "gran/71f8877cac84d38e.m4a",
  "The old routes are being wiped away, one by one. When you find this, ask the map makers why.": "gran/1f794c42ba25b7f4.m4a"
 }
}
